<title>ITALY: Milan airports May cargo traffic up 14.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Milan airports May cargo traffic up 14.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo traffic handled by Milan's airport system in May increased by 14 percent against the same period 1996,the airport authority said.</p>
<p>					Total Milan System</p>
<p>			   May	 Pct	   Jan/May     Pct</p>
<p>			   1997	Change	1997	  Change</p>
<p>Cargo (Tonnes)	 15,122    up 14.0	 73,580    up  7.0</p>
<p>Mail (Tonnes)	   1,194    up.22.9	  5,579    up 15.4</p>
<p>Passengers	  1,564,483    up 11.7    7,045,032    up 12.5</p>
<p>Aircraft Moves	 16,936    up  3.1	 80,834    up  6.0</p>
<p>LINATE</p>
<p>			   May	 Pct	    Jan/May    Pct</p>
<p>			   1997	Change	 1997	 Change</p>
<p>Cargo (Tonnes)	  5,411  down  8.3	 26,210  down  5.1</p>
<p>Mail (Tonnes)	   1,171    up 23.2	  5,450    up 15.6</p>
<p>Passengers	  1,277,224    up 13.1    5,571,723    up 14.3</p>
<p>Aircraft Moves	 14,035    up  1.8	 66,351    up  5.9</p>
<p>MALPENSA</p>
<p>			   May	Pct	    Jan/May     Pct</p>
<p>			   1997     Change			 Change</p>
<p>Cargo (Tonnes)	  9,711    up 31.9	 47,370    up 15.2</p>
<p>Mail (Tonnes)		24    up 10.4	    129    up  7.2</p>
<p>Passengers	    287,259    up  5.8    1,473,309    up  5.9</p>
<p>Aircraft Moves	  2,928  down  9.5	 14,483    up  6.5</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
<p>www.racs.com</p>
</text>
